## What this package is

This ZIP contains the client-specific **configuration** for one installation of the standard
PSA Edge appliance: Docker Compose files, the appliance configuration, a single-use enrollment
token and install / verify scripts. **It is not a Docker image.** The PSA Edge image is the same
for every client and is pulled from the registry (or built from source in development).

The appliance runs entirely on this host: the PSA integration, ticket processing and
synchronization, and its own PostgreSQL database. Ticket content and PSA credentials stay here.
The agent reports only approved health and metadata to the Control Plane over an outbound
connection.

## Quick start

Linux Docker host:

```bash
unzip {{archiveName}} && cd {{rootFolder}}
scripts/install.sh            # add --production for production hosts
scripts/verify.sh
```

Windows Docker host (Docker Desktop with Linux containers):

```powershell
Expand-Archive {{archiveName}}; Set-Location {{rootFolder}}
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts\install.ps1      # add -Production for production hosts
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts\verify.ps1
```

See **INSTALL.md** for prerequisites and details, and **UNINSTALL.md** to remove the appliance.

## Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `compose.yaml` | The appliance: database, migrations, API + local admin UI, PSA worker, agent, backups |
| `compose.production.yaml` | Production overrides: images pinned by digest, resource limits |
| `config/edge.json` | Non-secret appliance configuration (deployment identity, PSA settings, services) |
| `config/edge.env.template` | Optional local settings (port, image overrides, proxy) |
| `enrollment/enrollment.json` | **Single-use enrollment token.** Treat it like a password until the appliance has enrolled |
| `scripts/install.sh`, `scripts/install.ps1` | Generate this host's secrets, validate and start the appliance |
| `scripts/verify.sh`, `scripts/verify.ps1` | Check the local installation |
| `scripts/upgrade.sh`, `scripts/upgrade.ps1` | Apply an image upgrade staged by a signed remote command (the appliance has no Docker socket; the change happens on this host) |
| `scripts/uninstall.sh`, `scripts/uninstall.ps1` | Stop the appliance, or wipe it (`--wipe --confirm {{deploymentCode}}`) after the Control Plane decommissioned the deployment; always run by the host operator, never remotely |
| `scripts/edge-backup.sh` | Local database backups (run by the `edge-backup` service) |
| `manifest.json`, `CHECKSUMS.sha256` | File list and SHA-256 checksums (`sha256sum -c CHECKSUMS.sha256`) |

No permanent secret is included. Database passwords and the data-encryption key are generated on
this host by the install script, and PSA credentials are entered in the local admin UI.
